      "statusChangeID": "6068e69cd6e3a737fda1ce55",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "open",
      "value": "Let's swap this back to Open. That doesn't mean anything other than \"leaving stuff as planned for almost a year seems annoying\".\nThe way we chose to attack this problem is via improving how live data is handled-- in particular, using Friend Sync to update your friends in real time. It actually ends up working fairly well.\nOf course, just because something is the New Hotness doesn't mean it is without bugs! We're working on those.\nAs an aside, there's a definite psychological effect of simply having a \"refresh\" button available. I know I hit it in my browser even though I don't really need to.\nA good idea, even if it might be less needed nowadays.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
